{title: Fill Me Now}
{artist: Elwood H. Stokes / John R. Sweney}
{genre: Gospel}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Meditative}
{key: G}
{tempo: 130}
{time: 6/4}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score (Tabernacle Hymns Number Three (Chicago, Illinois: Tabernacle Publishing Company, 1950), # 63)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Hover o’er me, Holy Spirit,
[G]Bathe my trem[C]bling [G]heart and [D]brow;
[G]Fill me with Thy hallowed presence,
[G]Come, O come and [D7]fill [G]me now.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[D]Fill me now, [G]fill me now,
[C]Jesus, come [G]and fill me [D]now;
[G]Fill me with Thy hallowed presence,
[G]Come, O come, and [D7]fill me [G]now.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Thou canst fill me, gracious Spirit,
[G]Though I can[C]not [G]tell Thee [D]how;
[G]But I need Thee, greatly need Thee,
[G]Come, O come and [D7]fill [G]me now.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]I am weakness, full of weakness,
[G]At Thy sac[C]red [G]feet I [D]bow;
[G]Blest, divine, eternal Spirit,
[G]Fill with power and [D7]fill [G]me now.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]Cleanse and comfort, bless and save me,
[G]Bathe, O bathe [C]my [G]heart and [D]brow;
[G]Thou art comforting and saving,
[G]Thou art sweetly [D7]fill[G]ing now.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
